  === Complete Solutions
  #sol-item(1, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Commerce covers buying and selling plus the services that make both possible.
  ]

  #sol-item(2, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Each aid answers an obstacle: distance, risk, time, ignorance or payment.
  ]
  ]

  #sol-item(3, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Farming is primary production; the aids are the services around trade.
  ]

  #sol-item(4, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Primary extracts, secondary manufactures and constructs, tertiary serves.
  ]

  #sol-item(5, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It extracts raw material from nature, which is the definition of primary production.
  ]

  #sol-item(6, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The baker converts raw material into a finished good, creating form utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(7, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Transport is an aid to trade, and the aids are commercial occupations.
  ]

  #sol-item(8, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The professions serve the public without making or selling goods.
  ]

  #sol-item(9, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Construction assembles a structure and creates form utility, so it is secondary industry.
  ]

  #sol-item(10, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Record-keeping is an aid to trade; classification follows the job, not the firm.
  ]

  #sol-item(11, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Manufacture changes the shape or nature of a thing, which is form utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(12, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Moving goods to where they are wanted is place utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(13, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Holding goods until they are wanted is time utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(14, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The trader who buys and resells transfers ownership, which is possession utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(15, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Advertising tells the market that the good exists and what it does.
  ]

  #sol-item(16, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The first division is by place; wholesale and retail is the division within home trade.
  ]

  #sol-item(17, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The boundary of home trade is the national frontier.
  ]

  #sol-item(18, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The goods are imported only to leave again, so they are never consumed locally.
  ]

  #sol-item(19, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Visible trade is goods you can see; services are invisible trade.
  ]

  #sol-item(20, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The balance of trade counts goods only; invisibles appear in the balance of payments.
  ]

  #sol-item(21, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Each link moves the good closer to the final buyer and takes a margin.
  ]

  #sol-item(22, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The wholesaler buys from producers and sells in smaller lots to retailers.
  ]

  #sol-item(23, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The customer, not the size of the shop, decides the classification.
  ]

  #sol-item(24, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Ownership changes hands, which is possession utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(25, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Industry produces; commerce distributes.
  ]

  #sol-item(26, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Any activity that adds utility is production, which is why services count.
  ]

  #sol-item(27, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Difference in resources gives absolute advantage; relative cost gives comparative advantage.
  ]

  #sol-item(28, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Banking is an aid to trade; fishing, quarrying and weaving are industrial.
  ]

  #sol-item(29, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    He converts cloth into a garment, adding form utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(30, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Buying and selling without manufacture is trade, which is commerce.
  ]

  #sol-item(31, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It keeps produce until it is wanted, which is time utility.
  ]

  #sol-item(32, "B", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The wholesaler takes over functions the producer would otherwise carry.
  ]

  #sol-item(33, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Direct selling removes every middleman and every middleman's margin.
  ]

  #sol-item(34, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The functions survive; only the person performing them changes.
  ]

  #sol-item(35, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    It sells to the final consumer, which is retailing.
  ]

  #sol-item(36, "C", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The professions serve the public directly without making or trading goods.
  ]

  #sol-item(37, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    The balance of trade is a goods figure; services belong to the balance of payments.
  ]

  #sol-item(38, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Tertiary production provides services rather than goods.
  ]

  #sol-item(39, "A", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Commerce moves and sells; form utility belongs to manufacture.
  ]

  #sol-item(40, "D", dense: true, pad: 2.19pt)[
    Production is the creation of utility, at any of the three levels.
  ]

]

